          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP274 Calgary - Fish Creek Park [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A quick find inches to the ENE of the ankle-threatening hole. Thanks for another! &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="704099402">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP274 Calgary - Fish Creek Park [FOUND]

I began this morning with a plan to look for 4 caps In Fish Creek Provincial Park west of Macleod Trail and then look for another 4 in the park but east of Macleod Trail. This all unfolded according to plan. I still had a little time on my hands so decided to look for another pair in SE Calgary. I ended the day with a search for a geocache near the last cap. Thanks to ofth and vdD for setting up and maintaining these activities. I made a note of all the numbers and will add a few photos when I am near my photo software. This was brass cap #7 for today.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684213788">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1636194">behmSquad</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP274 Calgary - Fish Creek Park&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to an online heads up from Iron Phoenix, I knew this cap to be uncovered again.  I had visited this site previously and probed the ground in various places based on prior context photos.  Despite probing down 4-5 inches, I found nothing.  Visiting today, it was an easy find.  Surprisingly, it was found just where I did most of my probing.  Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684223364">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP274 - Calgary - Fish Creek Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, picking up ones we didn't get to earlier! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A busy day today and lots of walking, but a lot of fun!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; This was our first stop because we had the proper tools including the metal detector and we wanted to avenge the DNF earlier in the week!  We dug around a couple places, finding tin foil and a bolt, before finding the cap!  It was great to see that nice, shiny (mostly), circle in the ground!!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; I'm a bit behind on logging, but I swear I'll send the pics soon!! TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683845478">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP274 - Calgary - Fish Creek Park - Iron Phoenix and I got serious about finding this one. Metal detector, shovel, compass and patience were all packed. A visual inspection didn't locate the cap, so we broke out the metal detector and found a few things that weren't the cap before finally we found it. A little clearing and shovelling and the cap was revealed! That was a fun find. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
